<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Troupes de la Marine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Troupes de la Marine were independent companies of infantry under the French Ministry of the Marine, raised to defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s colonies and naval ports. From 1683 they formed the regular garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, and many of their officers were Canadian-born men skilled in frontier warfare alongside Native allies. They were reorganised in 1761 after the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/troupes-de-la-marine.jpg" alt="Troupes de la Marine" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: French School · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Disembarkation_of_50_soldiers_from_the_Karrer_Swiss_regiment_at_Louisbourg_on_the_Island_of_Cap-Breton_between_1722-33.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
